## 4. API Coverage

Current backend modules:

```text
Employees
Departments
Job Roles
Work Statuses
Attendance
Leave Types
Leave Requests
Performance Reviews
PIP
Training Programs
Employee Training
Candidates
Job Applications
Interviews
Job Offers
Analytics
```

## 5. Requirement Coverage

The backend currently provides implementation coverage for the major HR360 functional areas.

The only explicitly planned functional item in the current baseline is automated recruitment-to-employee transition.

## 6. Planned Backend Capability

```text
Accepted Job Offer
        |
        v
Automated Employee Creation
```

This remains planned and should not be represented as implemented until the functionality is developed and tested.

## 7. Traceability Governance

When backend functionality changes, the following artifacts should be reviewed:

1. BRD
2. Business Rules Catalogue
3. FRD
4. Product Backlog
5. Acceptance Criteria
6. API Documentation
7. Database Architecture
8. Test Cases
9. UAT
10. Traceability Matrix

## 8. Version Control

Backend documentation and implementation should be committed together at meaningful milestones.

Git history provides technical change traceability.

